# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for the test suite (ARCHIMEDES_SANITIZE=thread). The test
# binary reads this file itself (test/main.cpp defines __tsan_default_options), so ctest,
# Catch2's test discovery and direct runs all apply it.
#
# The SwiftShader CPU driver is a prebuilt, uninstrumented library: TSan cannot see the
# ordering inside it (its fiber scheduler, its own atomics, its JIT-compiled shaders), but
# it still records the calls it makes through intercepted functions (memcpy/memset into
# mapped and staging memory, its allocations, its pthread use). Those look unordered
# against everything else, so reports with a frame in the driver's module are suppressed.
# Every entry is scoped to that module. Never suppress acm:: symbols here: a report in
# Archimedes code is a finding to fix, not noise.
#
# Not called_from_lib: TSan aborts the process when a library it matched is unloaded, and
# acm::Instance unloads the directly loaded driver when it is destroyed.

race:libvk_swiftshader.so
deadlock:libvk_swiftshader.so
mutex:libvk_swiftshader.so
thread:libvk_swiftshader.so
